        <mxCell id="d7gty-hZnX5AW48Pm6Gb-48" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;li data-start=&quot;4659&quot; data-end=&quot;4721&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;4661&quot; data-end=&quot;4721&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;4765&quot; data-end=&quot;4790&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Payment Orchestrator:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt; single owner of payment workflow + status transitions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;4846&quot; data-end=&quot;4919&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;4848&quot; data-end=&quot;4919&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;4848&quot; data-end=&quot;4868&quot;&gt;Gateway Adapter:&lt;/strong&gt; isolates gateway differences (Razorpay vs Stripe).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;4920&quot; data-end=&quot;4968&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;4922&quot; data-end=&quot;4968&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;4922&quot; data-end=&quot;4942&quot;&gt;Webhook Handler:&lt;/strong&gt; secure gateway callbacks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;4969&quot; data-end=&quot;5038&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;4971&quot; data-end=&quot;5038&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="84" width="564" x="-60" y="-1494" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="d7gty-hZnX5AW48Pm6Gb-49" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;strong data-start=&quot;4971&quot; data-end=&quot;4996&quot; style=&quot;forced-color-adjust: none; box-shadow: none !important; color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: Helvetica; font-size: 12px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(27, 29, 30); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;&quot;&gt;Notification Service:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: Helvetica; font-size: 12px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(27, 29, 30); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; display: inline !important; float: none;&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;sends messages without slowing core flow.&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="36" width="384" x="480" y="-708" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="d7gty-hZnX5AW48Pm6Gb-51" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#6a00ff;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#3700CC;" value="Payment Orchestrator" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="156.28" x="40.61" y="-1370" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="d7gty-hZnX5AW48Pm6Gb-52" edge="1" parent="1" source="d7gty-hZnX5AW48Pm6Gb-60" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;exitX=0.153;exitY=-0.035;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;exitPerimeter=0;" value="">
          <mxGeometry height="50" relative="1" width="50" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="444" y="-732" />
            </Array>
            <mxPoint x="128" y="-1126" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="480" y="-732" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="d7gty-hZnX5AW48Pm6Gb-53" parent="1" style="shape=tape;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#a20025;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#6F0000;" value="Webhooh handler" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="110.25" width="216" x="39" y="-1193" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="d7gty-hZnX5AW48Pm6Gb-54" parent="1" style="shape=step;perimeter=stepPerimeter;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fixedSize=1;fillColor=#60a917;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#2D7600;" value="User / payment validator" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="91.5" width="144" x="-216" y="-1290" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="d7gty-hZnX5AW48Pm6Gb-55" parent="1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=none;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="438" width="438" x="-84" y="-852" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="d7gty-hZnX5AW48Pm6Gb-56" edge="1" parent="1" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;" value="">
          <mxGeometry height="50" relative="1" width="50" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="-264" y="-1236" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="-216" y="-1236" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="d7gty-hZnX5AW48Pm6Gb-57" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;h2 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Where interfaces can be used&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h2 data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;1.Gateway Abstraction&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot;&gt;&quot;The most critical place for an interface is the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;49&quot;&gt;Gateway Adapter&lt;/b&gt;. In my HLD, I would define a generic &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;102&quot;&gt;IPaymentGateway&lt;/code&gt; interface. This allows the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;145&quot;&gt;Payment Orchestrator&lt;/b&gt; to remain agnostic of whether we are using Stripe, Razorpay, or PayPal.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;The Interface:&lt;/b&gt; It would define methods like &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;44&quot;&gt;authorize()&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;57&quot;&gt;capture()&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;72&quot;&gt;refund()&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;5,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;The Benefit:&lt;/b&gt; If a gateway goes down or changes its API, I only need to update or swap the specific &#39;Adapter&#39; implementation. The core business logic in the Orchestrator never changes.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;hr data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;2. Decoupling the Storage Layer&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;8&quot;&gt;&quot;Next, I would use interfaces to separate my business logic from the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;8&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;69&quot;&gt;Persistence Layer&lt;/b&gt;. Instead of the services calling the database directly, they would interact with an &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;8&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;171&quot;&gt;IPaymentRepository&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;9,0,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;The Implementation:&lt;/b&gt; This allows us to swap a SQL-based implementation for a NoSQL one without a rewrite.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;9,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Testability:&lt;/b&gt; More importantly, it allows me to &#39;Mock&#39; the database during unit testing, ensuring our tests are fast and don&#39;t rely on a live DB connection.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;hr data-path-to-node=&quot;10&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 data-path-to-node=&quot;11&quot;&gt;3. Modular Validation Rules&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;12&quot;&gt;&quot;I would also apply interfaces to the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;12&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;38&quot;&gt;User/Payment Validator&lt;/b&gt; block. Instead of one giant &#39;if-else&#39; block, I’d use an &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;12&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;117&quot;&gt;IValidationRule&lt;/code&gt; interface.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;13&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;13,0,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;13,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;The Flow:&lt;/b&gt; I can create a list of rules like &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;13,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;44&quot;&gt;MinimumAmountValidator&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;13,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;68&quot;&gt;CurrencyValidator&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;13,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;91&quot;&gt;FraudScoreValidator&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;13,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;13,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Scalability:&lt;/b&gt; When the business team wants to add a new check (like &#39;limit payments from a specific region&#39;), I just implement a new class and add it to the validation pipeline.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;hr data-path-to-node=&quot;14&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 data-path-to-node=&quot;15&quot;&gt;4.Notificatios&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;16&quot;&gt;&quot;Finally, for the &lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;16&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;18&quot;&gt;Notification Service&lt;/b&gt;, I’d use an &lt;code data-path-to-node=&quot;16&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;51&quot;&gt;INotifier&lt;/code&gt; interface.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;17&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;17,0,0&quot;&gt;&lt;b data-path-to-node=&quot;17,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;The Benefit:&lt;/b&gt; The system just knows it needs to &#39;Notify&#39; the user. Whether that happens via Email, SMS, or Push Notification depends on which implementations are injected at runtime. This keeps the core payment flow lean and focused only on the money movement.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="720" width="564" x="-791.75" y="-672" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="d7gty-hZnX5AW48Pm6Gb-58" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d80073;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#A50040;" value="Kafka" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="36" width="204" x="48" y="-972" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="d7gty-hZnX5AW48Pm6Gb-59" edge="1" parent="1" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;" target="d7gty-hZnX5AW48Pm6Gb-55" value="">
          <mxGeometry height="50" relative="1" width="50" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="144" y="-924" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="38" y="-804" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="d7gty-hZnX5AW48Pm6Gb-60" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;li&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0,0&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;If the database is slow or the Orchestrator crashes mid-process, the user might get an error even if the gateway took their money.&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Message Queue (like RabbitMQ or Kafka) between the Validator and the Orchestrator. This ensures that once a payment request is validated, it is &quot;guaranteed&quot; to be processed eventually, even if a downstream service blips.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="96" width="564" x="180" y="-948" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
